This took a bit of snuffling through the docs, but here's what you do:

Assuming you're on a Unix box (I'd imagine the procedure is similar for
other OS's), you'll see in your NETHACKDIR a whole bunch of files, one
for each level you've visited, called something like '250Hawkmoon.13' where
250 is your user id, Hawkmoon's your player name, and 13's the level 
checkpointed in the file.  (I suspect the user id bit won't be there if you're
on a single-user machine....)

To use recover, just type 'recover <filename>', where filename is the name
of one of those checkpointed files I mentioned above.  That'll generate a save
file for you, so next time you start up nethack, you'll be left at the 
beginning of the level where the game crashed out.  This way, you only a couple
of hundred movees max - very handy!

